# Dependency and Supply Chain

- Add a dependency only when its value exceeds the maintenance, security,
  licensing, binary-size, and transitive-cost burden.
- Verify package identity, official source, maintained status, license, and
  compatible version before selection.
- Preserve lockfile integrity and review transitive and install-script changes.
- Prefer the smallest stable version movement that fixes the stated need.
- Read release notes and migration guidance; check runtime, build, API, and data
  compatibility.
- Keep credentials out of package configuration and disable unnecessary
  lifecycle execution.
- Run affected build and tests and retain a clear rollback path.
